+## DeepSeek Harness notes
+
+- **Parallelism comes from batching, not from a flag.** Issue every independent
+  dispatch **in the same message**; they run concurrently. One dispatch per message
+  runs them sequentially and defeats the whole pattern.
+- **Depth is 1 and enforced.** These workers cannot spawn subagents. Keep each
+  job self-contained — a nested dispatch fails with "subagent depth 2 exceeds
+  maxDepth 1".
+- **Hand artifacts over as files.** Everything pasted into a dispatch prompt stays
+  in your context and is re-read on every later turn. Write the brief to a file and
+  pass the path.
+- **Get each worker's report as its return value**, not as pasted console output.
+  Then verify by inspecting the files it changed — a summary is a claim, not
+  evidence.
+- Dispatch with `subagent`; use `subagent_fork` only when a worker genuinely needs
+  this conversation's prior turns.
+
 ## Common Mistakes
 
 **❌ Too broad:** "Fix all the tests" - agent gets lost
